// LLD of the format namespace (ds::format, DS-126, DS-398): every output of ds is a document. What is written and
// how it is written are two axes. A document describes itself once (IDescription) into the sink it is lent and knows
// no technology; a technology is a sink of emit. DescriptionFactory names the descriptions, one maker per document;
// emit's SinkFactory names the sinks; whoever asks for an output pairs them, description.describe(sink), and a pair
// ds does not write fails NotImplemented. To add a document: a description and its maker. To add a technology: a
// sink and its line in SinkFactory. What is no description yet is a writer behind IFormat<its document>, found by
// name in the map FormatFactory makes: the report and the answers as text (DS-399), the drawings (DS-400), the IR
// (DS-418) and the viewer's page.

package driftspec@ds {
  // every document ds writes, whichever module builds it: the package's, not the format module's
  requirement REQ-00106-3 {
    status: approved
    @refines SREQ-00013-1
    title: Each document ds writes shall be described once into the sink of the technology asked for, or written by a writer found by name, none of which reads the model, and a pair ds does not write shall fail NotImplemented
    text:
      What is written and how it is written are two axes. A document (the scene, a check's report, a
      query's answers, a diagram's layout and its cells) describes itself once, as records of named
      fields, lists and values, into the sink it is lent, and knows no technology; a technology is a
      sink of emit. One factory names the descriptions, one maker per document, and emit's SinkFactory
      names the sinks, found by the technology's name; whoever asks for an output pairs them, the
      description describing itself into the sink, so a new document or a new technology is one class
      and one maker and changes neither the other axis nor any door. What is no description yet (the
      report and the answers as text, a drawing in svg or text, the IR, and the viewer's page, which is
      the scene in JSON inside its template) is written by a writer behind one interface, found by name
      in the map its factory makes, with the options it is given (indented, the title, a reader's
      stylesheet, the identities a page opens framed on, whether a page is embedded and how tall, a
      width). Nothing of format reads the model, and every operation of format is a member of a class.
      The documents and the technologies need not make a complete matrix: a document asked in a
      technology ds does not write it in fails with NotImplemented, which names the document, the
      technology and what there is. The command line says it as bad usage (exit 2), though its
      options name only the pairs there are; the engine's interfaces let it through to their caller,
      the browser answers it as its error, and the Python face raises driftspec.NotImplemented, a
      NotImplementedError. A diagram asked of a workspace in a format that is none of its five fails
      so, and is not drawn as text instead.
      Every JSON document ds writes, a description's or not (the export, the engine's answers, the
      manual's page, the browser's answer), is written into one sink, emit's JsonSink, as ds has
      always written it: a record's fields in byte order, the escapes of nlohmann 3.11.3, indented
      by two spaces or compact, a double as the shortest digits that read back with its point kept
      (2.0) and null when it is not finite, and a text that is not UTF-8 refused. The sink keeps the
      document whole until it is taken, so a write that fails writes nothing. The render IR is
      written with nlohmann until it stops reading its own output back (DS-418).
    rationale:
      Owner, 2026-11-10 (DS-126): the scene, a diagram's IR, a query's answers and a check's
      findings are each written in several forms, each in its own way; one shape for all of them
      and the command line finding a format by name. Revision 2 (DS-394, DS-397, Owner
      2026-11-24): one streaming sink writes every JSON document in place of nlohmann's tree, byte
      for byte as before, so the export takes less time and memory and a technology is one class.
      Revision 3 (DS-394, DS-398, Owner 2026-11-24): each document described once and each
      technology a sink, extensible in both dimensions with no method per document on any catalogue
      and no interface per pair; a pair that is missing is a failure the caller handles, never
      something else written in its place.
    tags: format, render, scene, emit
    verification VER-00115-2 {
      status: approved
      title: Integration tests confirm the scene's formats are found by name, write the scene of a design, and the page becomes a frame when asked
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/format/test_formats_of_a_design.cpp::TestSceneFormatsOfADesign.EachFormatFoundByItsNameWritesTheSceneOfTheDesign
        tests/integration/ds/format/test_formats_of_a_design.cpp::TestSceneFormatsOfADesign.ThePageOfTheDesignIsAFrameCarryingItWholeWhenAskedToEmbed
    }
    verification VER-00116-2 {
      status: approved
      title: Integration tests confirm a diagram's five formats are found by name, the IR is written as it came unless asked to indent, and each drawing format draws the same diagram
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/format/test_formats_of_a_design.cpp::TestDiagramFormatsOfADesign.EveryFormatFoundByItsNameDrawsTheDiagramTheDesignDeclares
        tests/integration/ds/format/test_formats_of_a_design.cpp::TestDiagramFormatsOfADesign.EachDrawingFormatDrawsTheSameDiagramItsIrDescribes
    }
    verification VER-00117-3 {
      status: approved
      text: Revision 2 (DS-185) gives the formats of an answer and of a report a test each, named after their factory. Revision 3 (DS-137) verifies them over the answers and the report of a design.
      title: Integration tests confirm a query's answers and a check's report are written as text or JSON by name, and the report is built once from the model and read the same either way
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/format/test_formats_of_a_design.cpp::TestTextFormatsOfADesign.TheAnswersOfAQueryAreWrittenAsTextOrJsonByName
        tests/integration/ds/format/test_formats_of_a_design.cpp::TestTextFormatsOfADesign.TheReportOfTheCheckIsBuiltOnceAndReadsTheSameAsTextAndAsJson
    }
    verification VER-00222-1 {
      status: approved
      title: Integration tests confirm every JSON document ds writes of a design, through a checked sink and through the doors, has its fields in byte order and reads back as nlohmann writes it, and a write that fails writes nothing
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/emit/test_json_of_a_design.cpp::TestJsonOfADesign.EveryWriterLentACheckedSinkWritesWhatNlohmannWrote
        tests/integration/ds/emit/test_json_of_a_design.cpp::TestJsonOfADesign.EveryAnswerOfTheDoorsReadsBackAsNlohmannWritesIt
        tests/integration/ds/emit/test_json_of_a_design.cpp::TestJsonOfADesign.AWriteThatFailsHalfWayWritesNothingOfTheDocument
    }
    verification VER-00225-1 {
      status: approved
      title: Integration tests confirm the design of ds keeps the rules of format, and is told when a description names a technology, anything but its factory names a description or a writer, format writes a function, a description uses another or a writer reads the model
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_format_principles.cpp::TestFormatPrinciples.TheDesignOfDsKeepsTheRulesOfFormat
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_format_principles.cpp::TestFormatPrinciples.ADescriptionThatNamesTheJsonSinkIsTold
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_format_principles.cpp::TestFormatPrinciples.ADescriptionThatMakesItsOwnSinkIsTold
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_format_principles.cpp::TestFormatPrinciples.ADoorThatNamesADescriptionIsTold
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_format_principles.cpp::TestFormatPrinciples.AnotherFactoryThatNamesADescriptionIsTold
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_format_principles.cpp::TestFormatPrinciples.AClassThatNamesAWriterIsTold
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_format_principles.cpp::TestFormatPrinciples.AFunctionInFormatIsTold
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_format_principles.cpp::TestFormatPrinciples.ADescriptionThatUsesAnotherIsTold
        tests/integration/ds/check/test_format_principles.cpp::TestFormatPrinciples.AWriterThatReadsTheModelIsTold
    }
    verification VER-00226-1 {
      status: approved
      title: Integration tests confirm a diagram asked of a workspace in a format ds does not write fails NotImplemented, naming the document and the technology, in C++ and as driftspec.NotImplemented in Python, and the engine's render draws as it always has
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/api/test_workspace_of_a_design.cpp::TestWorkspace.ADiagramAskedInAFormatDsDoesNotWriteFailsNotImplemented
        tests/integration/python/test_workspace.py::TestNotImplemented::test_a_diagram_asked_in_a_format_the_engine_does_not_write_raises_not_implemented
    }
  }

  module format {
    // ---- the principles, as rules ----------------------------------------------------------
    rule formats-read-no-model {
      title: a description or a writer writes the document it is given; nothing of format reads the model
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      for class c in driftspec@ds@format
      never depends(c, driftspec@ds@model::Model)
    }

    rule no-format-uses-another {
      title: descriptions and writers are siblings: none uses another; what two of them need goes in common, and a writer that carries a document asks its factory for the description
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      for class a in driftspec@ds@format, class b in driftspec@ds@format
      where a != b, a inherits x, b inherits y
      never depends(a, b)
    }

    rule common-classes-know-no-format {
      title: what the writers share knows none of them, nor any description (DS-397)
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      for class c in driftspec@ds@format::common
      never depends(c, x), x in driftspec@ds@format, not x in driftspec@ds@format::common
    }

    rule descriptions-know-no-technology {
      title: a description names nothing of emit but the interface of the sinks, so it knows no technology and makes no sink of its own (DS-398)
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      for class d in driftspec@ds@format, class t in driftspec@ds@emit
      where d inherits driftspec@ds@format::IDescription, t != driftspec@ds@emit::ISink
      never depends(d, t)
    }

    definition of-the-factory(x, f) {
      title: x is part of the factory f, a behaviour of one of its members, or a box that holds it: what names what f makes
      if x in f, f is class
      if x behaviour-of m, m in f, f is class
      if f in x, f is class
    }

    rule descriptions-are-named-by-their-factory {
      title: nothing but DescriptionFactory names a description, so whoever asks for a document holds it as an IDescription (DS-398)
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      for class d in driftspec@ds@format
      where d inherits driftspec@ds@format::IDescription
      never depends(x, d), x in driftspec@ds, x != d, not x in d, x != driftspec@ds@format::DescriptionFactory, not of-the-factory(x, driftspec@ds@format::DescriptionFactory)
    }

    rule writers-are-named-by-their-factory {
      title: nothing but FormatFactory names a writer, so whoever asks for one finds it by name and holds it as an IFormat (DS-398)
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      for class w in driftspec@ds@format, class i in driftspec@ds@format
      where w inherits i, name(i) = "IFormat"
      never depends(x, w), x in driftspec@ds, x != w, not x in w, x != driftspec@ds@format::FormatFactory, not of-the-factory(x, driftspec@ds@format::FormatFactory)
    }

    rule format-operations-belong-to-classes {
      title: no function is written in the format module, so every operation of format is a member of a class (DS-398)
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      for function f in driftspec@ds@format
      never f in driftspec@ds@format
    }

    // ---- what is written: each document described once, knowing no technology ----------------
    // THE EXTENSION POINT of the documents: a document describes itself into the sink it is lent
    class IDescription {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      + ~IDescription()
      + abstract describe(out_sink: emit::ISink) -> void fails NotImplemented   // a sink that cannot write what it is given fails
    }

    // the scene, for the viewer: every record an array whose columns fields names, a node, a behaviour or a link named
    // by its index; ds render -f json, and the scene inside the viewer's page
    class SceneDescription : IDescription {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      - refs document_: scene::SceneDocument
      - owns nodeAt_: std::map<std::string, int>
      - owns behaviourAt_: std::map<std::string, int>
      - owns requirementAt_: std::map<std::string, int>
      - owns landing_: scene::Map                    // where a link's sequence lands: the behaviour it is
      + SceneDescription(document: scene::SceneDocument)
      + describe(out_sink: emit::ISink) -> void fails NotImplemented
      - node(id: std::string) -> int
      - requirement(id: std::string) -> int
      - behaviourOf(sequence: std::string) -> int
      - static box(b: layout::Box, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> void
      - static texts(texts: std::vector<std::string>, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> void
      - static pairs(pairs: std::vector<std::pair<std::string, std::string>>, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> void
    }

    // a check's report as one record of its findings and counts, the one shape every caller reads: ds check --json,
    // the api, and the browser's answer, which carries it as one of its fields
    class ReportDescription : IDescription {
      @requirement SREQ-00002-1
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      - refs report_: check::Report
      + ReportDescription(report: check::Report)
      + describe(out_sink: emit::ISink) -> void fails NotImplemented
      - findings(findings: std::vector<model::Finding>, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> void   // code, location, message, the severity's name
    }

    // ds query --json: a list of records of the same three fields
    class AnswersDescription : IDescription {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      - refs answers_: std::vector<query::Answer>
      + AnswersDescription(answers: std::vector<query::Answer>)
      + describe(out_sink: emit::ISink) -> void fails NotImplemented
    }

    // ds render -f layout: where each node and route goes, in cells, for hosts that draw themselves
    class LayoutDescription : IDescription {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      - refs ir_: render::IrText
      - owns metrics_: render::Metrics
      - width_: int
      + LayoutDescription(ir: render::IrText, theme: theme::Theme, width: int)   // measured as the theme measures text in a terminal (DS-393)
      + describe(out_sink: emit::ISink) -> void fails NotImplemented
      - placed(document: render::IrDocument, part: std::string, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> void   // a part names itself
    }

    // ds render -f cells: the terminal's coloured cells
    class CellsDescription : IDescription {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      - refs ir_: render::IrText
      - owns text_: render::Text
      - width_: int
      + CellsDescription(ir: render::IrText, theme: theme::Theme, width: int)    // drawn in the theme (DS-393)
      + describe(out_sink: emit::ISink) -> void fails NotImplemented
    }

    // THE DOCUMENT AXIS: the one place that names the descriptions, one maker per document. A door asks it for the
    // description, asks emit's SinkFactory for the sink and pairs them; a description refers to the document it is
    // given, which outlives it
    class DescriptionFactory {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      + static scene(document: scene::SceneDocument) -> std::unique_ptr<IDescription>
      + static report(report: check::Report) -> std::unique_ptr<IDescription>
      + static answers(answers: std::vector<query::Answer>) -> std::unique_ptr<IDescription>
      + static layout(ir: render::IrText, theme: theme::Theme, width: int) -> std::unique_ptr<IDescription>
      + static cells(ir: render::IrText, theme: theme::Theme, width: int) -> std::unique_ptr<IDescription>
    }

    // ---- what is no description yet: writers found by name ----------------------------------
    // what every writer is given besides its document
    dataclass FormatOptions {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      + pretty: bool
      + title: std::string
      + css: std::string
      + focus: std::vector<std::string>
      + embed: bool
      + height: int
      + width: int
      + color: bool
    }

    // THE EXTENSION POINT of the writers: IFormat<D>, D the document a writer writes; each names its document in its
    // base, as the code does (DS-18). Whoever asks for the output lends the sink: the viewer's page describes the
    // scene into it; a writer of text leaves it alone (DS-397)
    class IFormat<D> {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      + ~IFormat()
      + abstract name() -> std::string
      + abstract write(document: D, options: FormatOptions, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> std::string
    }

    // ---- what the writers share: knows no description or writer, never reads the model -------
    module common {
      // text deflated (zlib) and written in base64: how the scene and the viewer travel inside a page
      class Packing {
        @requirement REQ-00075-5
        + static pack(text: std::string) -> std::string
        + static unpack(packed: std::string) -> std::string   // empty when it holds no pack
      }
    }

    // the one place that names the writers, keyed by name; each goes when its document is described and its
    // technology is a sink
    class FormatFactory {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      + static scene() -> std::map<std::string, std::unique_ptr<IFormat<scene::SceneDocument>>>   // html
      + static diagram(theme: theme::Theme) -> std::map<std::string, std::unique_ptr<IFormat<render::IrText>>>   // ir, svg, text
      + static answers() -> std::map<std::string, std::unique_ptr<IFormat<std::vector<query::Answer>>>>   // text
      + static report() -> std::map<std::string, std::unique_ptr<IFormat<check::Report>>>   // text
    }

    // ds render -f html: the viewer as one page, or that page as an iframe when options.embed asks. It is no
    // technology: it is the scene in JSON inside its template
    class ViewerPage : IFormat<scene::SceneDocument> {
      @requirement REQ-00070-1
      @requirement REQ-00071-2
      @requirement REQ-00077-1
      @requirement REQ-00092-3
      + name() -> std::string
      + write(document: scene::SceneDocument, options: FormatOptions, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> std::string
      + static viewerTemplate() -> std::string    // viewer/scene.html compiled in, with the places the scene fills
      // the scene described and the identities it opens framed on, written one after the other into the compact sink lent
      - static page(document: scene::SceneDocument, title: std::string, css: std::string, focus: std::vector<std::string>, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> std::string
      - static frame(page: std::string, title: std::string, height: int) -> std::string
    }

    // ds render -f ir: the IR as it came, indented when asked
    class DiagramIr : IFormat<render::IrText> {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      + name() -> std::string
      + write(document: render::IrText, options: FormatOptions, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> std::string
    }

    // ds render -f svg
    class DiagramSvg : IFormat<render::IrText> {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      - owns svg_: render::Svg
      + DiagramSvg(theme: theme::Theme)            // drawn in the theme (DS-393)
      + name() -> std::string
      + write(document: render::IrText, options: FormatOptions, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> std::string
    }

    // ds render -f text: boxes in characters for a terminal
    class DiagramText : IFormat<render::IrText> {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      - owns text_: render::Text
      + DiagramText(theme: theme::Theme)            // drawn in the theme (DS-393)
      + name() -> std::string
      + write(document: render::IrText, options: FormatOptions, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> std::string
    }

    // ds query: kind  identity  detail, one answer per line
    class AnswersText : IFormat<std::vector<query::Answer>> {
      @requirement REQ-00106-3
      + name() -> std::string
      + write(document: std::vector<query::Answer>, options: FormatOptions, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> std::string
    }

    // ds check: each finding where it is, then the counts
    class ReportText : IFormat<check::Report> {
      @requirement SREQ-00002-1
      + name() -> std::string
      + write(document: check::Report, options: FormatOptions, out_sink: emit::ISink) -> std::string
    }

    // ---- what each factory makes (DS-451: a factory names its products) -----------------------
    sequence DescriptionFactory::scene {
      local description: SceneDescription
      return description
    }

    sequence DescriptionFactory::report {
      local description: ReportDescription
      return description
    }

    sequence DescriptionFactory::answers {
      local description: AnswersDescription
      return description
    }

    sequence DescriptionFactory::layout {
      local description: LayoutDescription
      return description
    }

    sequence DescriptionFactory::cells {
      local description: CellsDescription
      return description
    }

    sequence FormatFactory::scene {
      local page: ViewerPage
      return writers
    }

    sequence FormatFactory::diagram {
      local ir: DiagramIr
      local svg: DiagramSvg
      local text: DiagramText
      return writers
    }

    sequence FormatFactory::answers {
      local text: AnswersText
      return writers
    }

    sequence FormatFactory::report {
      local text: ReportText
      return writers
    }

    // the scene described into the sink lent and taken as one document, then the focus; the page is the viewer with
    // both inside
    sequence ViewerPage::page {
      -> DescriptionFactory::scene(document) -> description
      -> description.describe(out_sink)
      -> out_sink.result() -> json
      -> common::Packing::pack(json) -> packed
      -> viewerTemplate() -> page
      -> out_sink.result() -> framed
      return page
    }

    sequence ViewerPage::write {
      -> page(document, title, css, focus, out_sink) -> written
      opt embedded / framed {
        -> frame(written, title, height) -> iframe
        return iframe
      }
      return written
    }
  }
}

diagram CL_Format {
  kind: class
  include: driftspec@ds@format::*
}
